<title>GHANA: Ghana ends 1996/97 main crop cocoa season.</title>
<headline>Ghana ends 1996/97 main crop cocoa season.</headline>
<dateline>ACCRA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ghana will end its 1996/97 main crop cocoa purchasing season at the close of business on Thursday but final returns on purchases will be accepted until April 17, a Ghana Cocoa Board (COCOBOD) statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;(The April 17 deadline) is to assist the Produce Buying Company Limited and other licensed buying companies to obtain their final returns from their up-country stations, &quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The light crop season would begin at the end of April or early May, it added.</p>
<p>--Matthew Bunce, Abidjan newsroom + 225 21 90 90</p>
</text>
